course: dictionary
lesson: 11670
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word asset is a good example. «She is an asset to the team» means she is useful and helps the team do well. Here, an asset is a person.
explain: In money lessons, asset means something different. «The family listed their house, savings and car as assets.» These are things they own that are worth money. The words house, savings and car tell you this is about money, not about helping.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is this sentence about helping, money or games? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. If you are still unsure, a dictionary shows each meaning, numbered, so you can pick the one that fits.
fact: Asset means a person or thing that is useful or valuable.
fact: In money, assets are things a person or company owns that are worth money.
fact: Examples of money assets are houses, land, savings and machines.
fact: Asset is a noun, and its plural is assets.
fact: In games, game assets are the pictures and sounds that the game uses.
exercise: «She is an asset to the team.» What does asset mean here? | *Someone useful who helps the team | A debt that must be paid back | A small bag for sports kit | A game with lots of pictures
exercise: «The company sold some of its assets to pay what it owed.» What are assets in this sentence? | Pictures on its website | Bills the company has to pay | *Things the company owns that are worth money | People who work for the company
exercise: What is the plural of asset? | assetts | assetes | asset's | *assets
test: «The designer saved all the game assets in one folder.» What does asset mean here? | *The pictures and sounds used in the game | A prize for the best score | A type of computer | A player who wins every level
test: Mia says, «My dad is an asset at work.» What does Mia mean? | Dad is always late for work | Dad has a new car | Dad owns a lot of money | *Dad is very useful and helps at work
exam: «The bank asked for a list of the family's assets.» What does asset mean here? | People who help the family | *Things the family owns that are worth money | Jobs that pay well | Pictures in a computer game
